1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,369
Before we write a single line of code, what actually happens when someone pays a shop online with a card?

2
00:00:05,369 --> 00:00:12,059
Five players are involved: the buyer, the shop, the acquirer bank, the processing center, and the issuer bank.

3
00:00:12,059 --> 00:00:17,880
The acquirer is the shop's bank, the one we are building, and the issuer is the bank that gave the buyer their card.

4
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:25,607
Every shop gets a terminal at the acquirer, identified by a merchant ID and a terminal ID, the MID and TID.

5
00:00:25,607 --> 00:00:31,511
When the buyer pays, the acquirer sends an authorization through the processing center to the issuer.

6
00:00:31,511 --> 00:00:37,261
The issuer checks the balance and places a hold, so the money is reserved but not yet moved.

7
00:00:37,261 --> 00:00:41,428
Then the acquirer captures the hold, and the payment becomes final.

8
00:00:41,428 --> 00:00:46,904
A reversal cancels a payment before settlement, and a refund sends money back after it.

9
00:00:46,904 --> 00:00:51,523
At the end of the day, the processing center settles all payments with the acquirer.

10
00:00:51,523 --> 00:00:56,023
The acquirer keeps its commission and pays the shop the rest by the next banking day.

11
00:00:56,023 --> 00:01:05,523
These words, authorization, capture, MID, TID, and settlement, will name the classes we build in every episode that follows.

